From 7f6d7640d1494da1404a794d6a2a8dcd269fcd8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Al <al@example.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:28:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sync): harden multi-device sync and settings sync

Sync engine
- delete propagates across devices via server-side tombstones
- stock is applied as idempotent delta (adjust_stock RPC), never overwritten
- updated_at set by DB trigger; checkpoint = max server updated_at (no clock skew)
- queue ordered by (createdAt, seq); failed docs no longer block the queue;
  permanent failures go to dead-letter after 5 tries
- realtime: no dropped signals while fetching, auto-resubscribe, 60s poll fallback
- sync_metadata table + RLS + realtime publication in migration

Settings
- empty remote values are respected (no resurrection from signup metadata)
- device-specific fields (printer, receipt, images) stay local
- offline edits kept as pending patch and flushed on reconnect
- diff-only upserts, echo/stale realtime events ignored
- notifier no longer resets to defaults on auth token refresh

Security
- PIN stored as salted PBKDF2 hash (legacy plaintext auto-migrated)
- forgot-password uses verify_reset_identity RPC instead of anon SELECT
